Implement or repair the following tool. Satisfy every requirement.

SPECIFICATION
{
  "name": "deterministic_canonicalize_and_filter",
  "when_to_use": "When processing a list of extracted entity records where names vary (aliases) and relations contain mixed functional descriptions (direct action vs. regulation).",
  "requirements": "1. Initialize an empty dictionary for canonical entities. 2. For each record in input: a. Determine the canonical name: Check if 'name' or any 'alias' exists in 'canonicalization_map'. If yes, use the mapped value. If no, use 'name' lowercased and stripped as the key. b. Check 'relation' for 'action_keywords' (case-insensitive substring match). If none found, skip record. c. Check 'relation' for 'exclusion_keywords'. If found AND no 'action_keywords' found, skip record. (Note: If both are present, action_keywords take precedence). d. If record passes, add to the dictionary under the canonical key: merge 'aliases' (deduplicated), append 'evidence_id', append 'qualifiers', and store the first valid 'relation' as 'primary_relation'. 3. Convert dictionary to list and return.\nInvariants: [\"Every output entity has a unique canonical_name.\", \"Every output entity has at least one evidence_id.\", \"Every output entity's primary_relation contains at least one action_keyword.\", \"No output entity is included if its relation only contains exclusion_keywords and no action_keywords.\"]\nEdge cases: [\"If a record has no aliases and is not in the map, it is treated as its own canonical entity.\", \"If a record's relation contains both action and exclusion keywords, it is included (action takes precedence).\", \"If multiple records map to the same canonical name, their evidence IDs and qualifiers are merged into a single list.\"]",
  "input_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "records": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "aliases": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "relation": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "evidence_id": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "qualifiers": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "name",
            "relation",
            "evidence_id"
          ]
        }
      },
      "canonicalization_map": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Runtime map of aliases to canonical names. Keys are aliases, values are canonical names."
      },
      "action_keywords": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "description": "List of keywords indicating direct performance of the target action."
      },
      "exclusion_keywords": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "description": "List of keywords indicating regulation or association without direct performance."
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "records",
      "canonicalization_map",
      "action_keywords",
      "exclusion_keywords"
    ]
  },
  "output_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "canonical_entities": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "canonical_name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "aliases": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "merged_evidence_ids": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "primary_relation": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "merged_qualifiers": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "canonical_name",
            "merged_evidence_ids",
            "primary_relation"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "canonical_entities"
    ]
  },
  "limitations": "Relies on the provided canonicalization map and keyword lists; cannot infer relationships not explicitly stated in the text or map.",
  "description": "Deterministic transformation of supplied structured annotations. Semantic processing has already finished outside this Python function."
}
Implement run(payload:dict). Do not infer medical facts; only execute the documented operation. Preserve inputs and deterministic JSON output. Raise ValueError for invalid inputs according to this specification. Nonempty docstring must state limitations. No files, network, model calls, dynamic imports or import-time execution.

